# UI Components and Design Patterns

## Component Library
Uses **shadcn/ui** components with Tailwind CSS for consistent styling.

### Key UI Components Used
- `Button` - Primary actions and navigation
- `Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle, CardDescription` - Content containers
- `Input` - Form inputs and text fields
- `Select, SelectContent, SelectItem, SelectTrigger, SelectValue` - Dropdown menus
- `ScrollArea` - Scrollable content regions
- `ResizablePanel, ResizablePanelGroup, ResizableHandle` - Layout panels

### Icon System
Uses **Lucide React** icons consistently:
- `Settings` (SettingsIcon) - Settings sections
- `Terminal` - Developer tools
- `Brain` - AI provider settings
- `Mic` - Voice/audio settings
- `MonitorSpeaker` - Main interface
- `ArrowLeft` - Navigation back
- `PanelLeftOpen/PanelLeftClose` - Panel toggles

## Layout Patterns
### Three-Panel Layout Structure
```tsx
// Main content conditional rendering
{currentView === "settings" ? (
  <Settings onNavigateToDevTools={...} onNavigateToChat={...} />
) : currentView === "devtools" ? (
  <DevToolsPanel />
) : (
  <ResizablePanelGroup>
    <ResizablePanel>Chat</ResizablePanel>
    <ResizableHandle />
    <ResizablePanel>DevTools</ResizablePanel>
  </ResizablePanelGroup>
)}
```

### Settings Section Pattern
Each settings section follows this structure:
```tsx
<Card>
  <CardHeader>
    <CardTitle className="flex items-center gap-2">
      <Icon size={20} />
      Section Title
    </CardTitle>
    <CardDescription>Section description</CardDescription>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent className="space-y-4">
    {/* Form controls */}
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

## Navigation Components
### Header Pattern
- Always shows current view context
- Conditional back button for non-chat views
- Server status indicator
- Action buttons (dev panel toggle)

### Navigation Props Pattern
Components that need navigation use callback props:
```tsx
interface ComponentProps {
  onNavigateToDevTools?: () => void;
  onNavigateToChat?: () => void;
}
```

## State Management
### View State
- Use `AppView` type for view switching
- Store in component state, not global state
- Handle transitions through event listeners

### Form State
- Local component state for form data
- Sync with backend through Tauri commands
- Show loading states during async operations

## Styling Guidelines
- Use `cn()` utility for conditional classes
- Follow Tailwind spacing scale: `gap-2`, `space-y-4`, `p-4`
- Use semantic color classes: `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-muted`
- Apply consistent border radius and shadows
